+# Moh (99,66) p.209 branch audit
+
+Frozen input gate: MECHANICAL.  I generated `/tmp/moh9966.sha256` from
+`xmodel/moh9966-branches-gpt55-20260903.run.v2` with `awk` and ran
+`sha256sum -c`.  All ten charged inputs in `/tmp/jc2-lane.4zSf7l/inputs`
+matched.  No digit was retyped into the check.
+
+Page images: SOURCE-READ.  Printed Moh pp.207--211 are PDF pages 68--72.
+Rendered with `pdftoppm -r 200 -png` into:
+
+```text
+box/moh9966-20260903/pages/moh_p207_pdf68.png
+box/moh9966-20260903/pages/moh_p208_pdf69.png
+box/moh9966-20260903/pages/moh_p209_pdf70.png
+box/moh9966-20260903/pages/moh_p210_pdf71.png
+box/moh9966-20260903/pages/moh_p211_pdf72.png
+box/moh9966-20260903/pages/moh_pp207_211_ocr.txt
+```
+
+No ledger edits; no `jc2-lean`; no `ideation-*` files.  Driver/results:
+`box/moh9966-20260903/moh9966_branch_driver.py`,
+`box/moh9966-20260903/moh9966_branch_results.json`, and the emitted
+Singular scripts under `box/moh9966-20260903/systems/`.
+
+## Source Transcription
+
+SOURCE-READ p.207: Appendix II starts from the four possible degree classes
+`(64,68)`, `(84,56)`, `(75,50)`, `(99,66)`.  For the first three only, Moh
+uses Prop.6.4 and says `u_3 = d_3 - v_3 = 1`.  The displayed transformed table
+for those first three has columns
+`n, m=-M_1, M_2, V_2, delta_2, delta_1, Jacobian`.
+
+SOURCE-READ p.208 method, first row template:
+
+```text
+bar sigma = t^{-1} + a_0 + a_1 t + a_2 t^2 + pi t^(11/4)
+
+bar g(y)=h(y)^4 + alpha_1(y)h(y)^3 + alpha_2(y)h(y)^2
+       + alpha_3(y)h(y) + alpha_4(y)
+bar f(y)=h(y)^3 + beta_2(y)h(y) + beta_3(y)
+
+h(y) = the fourth approximate root of bar f(y)
+deg_y alpha_i(y) <= 3,  deg_y beta_i(y) <= 3
+ord alpha_i(sigma) >= i(-1/4),  ord alpha_i(bar sigma) >= i(-1/4)
+ord beta_i(sigma) >= i(-1/4),   ord beta_i(bar sigma) >= i(-1/4)
+ord h(sigma) >= -1/4,           ord h(bar sigma) >= -1/4
+
+h(x,y)=y^3(y-x)+b_1 y^3+b_2 y^2+b_3 y+b_4
+      =y A(x,y)+b_4
+      =y^2 B(x,y)+b_3 y+b_4
+alpha_1 is a constant
+alpha_2=c_1 A+c_2,              beta_2=c_3 A+c_4
+alpha_3=c_5 A+c_6 B+c_7,        beta_3=c_8 A+c_9 B+c_10
+alpha_4=c_11 A+c_12 B+c_13(y-x)
+```
+
+SOURCE-READ p.208--209 eta reduction for the same template:
+
+```text
+f=eta^-12
+g=eta^-16 + a_1 eta^-12 + a_2 eta^-8 + a_3 eta^-4 + a_4 + ...
+(f,g) -> (f - (3/4)a_3, g - a_1 f - a_4)
+g=eta^-16 + a_2 eta^-8 + terms in eta with positive exponents
+f=h^3+beta_2 h+beta_3=h^3(1+beta_2 h^-2+beta_3 h^-3)
+
+g=h^4 + (4/3)(beta_2 h^2+beta_3 h)
+  + (2/9)(beta_2^2+2 gamma) - (4/81)delta + a_2 h^2
+beta_2 beta_3 = gamma h + gamma*,  beta_2^3 = delta h^2 + delta*
+deg_y gamma* < deg h = 4,  deg_y delta* < deg h^2 = 8
+```
+
+Moh then says the coefficient count is reduced to 10.  TYPE: this
+ten-coefficient final system is not printed.
+
+SOURCE-READ p.209, fourth `(99,66)` setup:
+
+```text
+sigma = a_{-1} t^-1 + a_0 + a_1 t + pi t^2
+g(sigma) = g_sigma(pi) t^-18 + ...
+
+g_sigma(pi) is either a power of a linear polynomial or the 9-th power
+of a cubic polynomial with precisely two roots.
+```
+
+Branch A, SOURCE-READ p.209:
+
+```text
+n=27, m=-M_1=18, M_2=21, V_2=8, delta_2=-1, delta_1=0,
+Jacobian = X^4.
+```
+
+Moh immediately says the above method reduces the number of coefficients to
+10.  The monomials and equations for those 10 coefficients are omitted.
+
+Branch B, SOURCE-READ p.209--210:
+
+```text
+Omega: x -> x^-1,  y -> a_0 + a_1 x + a_2 x^2 + y x^3
+Omega(f(x,y))       = x^6 y^18 + ...
+Omega(g(x,y))       = x^9 y^27 + ...
+Omega(T_2^psi(x,y)) = x^5 y^15 + ...
+Omega(T_3^psi(x,y)) = x^15 y^40 + ...
+J_{x,y}(Omega f(x,y), Omega g(x,y)) = x
+```
+
+Page 210 says that a discussion of solutions of `Omega(g(x,y))=0` in
+`k((x^-1))` and `k((y^-1))`, with a slightly modified version of the above
+method, reduces the computation to only 11 variables.  TYPE: the 11 variables,
+monomial support, and equations are not printed.
+
+SOURCE-READ p.210--211: the displayed contradiction is for the different
+case `(n,m,M_2,V_2)=(15,10,11,3)`, not for either `(99,66)` branch.  It uses
+`f=h^2+2 beta`, `beta^2=alpha h+gamma`,
+`beta^3=(3 gamma+a)h^2+epsilon h+delta`, the form
+`h=(y^2-x^2+a_1 y+a_2 x+a_3)y^3+(a_4x+a_5)y^2+(a_6x+a_7)y+a_8`,
+`beta=a_9A+a_10y+a_11x+a_12`, then splits `a_9=0` and `a_9 != 0`.
+The final sentence is the blanket assertion that all other cases compute
+directly as above.
+
+## Conditions Used
+
+EXACT-ARITHMETIC from the p.202 row and Def.5.1:
+
+```text
+n=99, m=66, s=3
+M_1..M_3=(-66,77,97)
+d_1..d_4=(99,33,11,1)
+V_2,V_3=(8,8)
+u_3=d_3-V_3=3,  v_3/u_3=8/3
+major (delta_1,delta_2,delta_3)=(4/9,1/3,-1)
+```
+
+TYPE: `delta_2=1/3` is a major-disc radius, not the actual minor radius
+`delta_2^*`.  The p.209 displayed `sigma` is a radius-2 `g`-probe.  Its order
+is `ord g(sigma)=(99/11)(3*2-8)=-18`, matching the printed `t^-18`.
+
+SOURCE-READ via charged inputs:
+Def.5.1 gives the radii and D1 order rule; see
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.4zSf7l/inputs/appendix2-compiler-grok46-20260903.md:205`.
+The monomial valuation is `val(x^i y^j)=-i+delta_1 j`, so
+`h` allows `i <= delta_1(j+1)` and `beta` allows
+`i <= delta_1(j+d')`.  The two-point leading form for `delta_2=-1` is
+`y^{V_2}(y-x)` when `u'=1`; see lines 213--220 of the same frozen report.
+
+Lemma 2.1 and the Jacobian enter the constructed systems as
+`J(f,g)=c x^k`, `c != 0`.  The Prop.4.6 root-polynomial ODE and its
+Jacobian origin are source-audited in
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.4zSf7l/inputs/prop55k-opus5-20260903.md:122-136`.
+
+TYPE: In the two-root cubic branch, the two distinct roots of `g_sigma`
+give two `g` roots with contact exactly 2, hence `delta_2^* <= 2 < 8/3`.
+Therefore Prop.6.3 is not licensed there.  This is not a coefficient kill.
+In the linear branch, `g` has one distinct probe root; p.209 gives no common
+`T_i^psi` probe profile, so the actual combined `delta_2^*` remains
+undetermined.
+
+## Reconstructed Systems
+
+Branch A computable predecessor.  I used the source-checked two-point
+`d'=2,e'=3` A/B system on Moh's transformed row `(27,18;M_2=21,V_2=8;k=4)`.
+This is not the omitted ten-coefficient eta-reduced display; it is the
+13-coefficient plus Jacobian-constant predecessor under the p.208/p.210
+A/B reading.  TYPE: Moh does not print enough to verify that his omitted
+ten-coefficient eta system is exactly a specialization of this predecessor,
+so the computed kill is reported for the predecessor, not promoted to the
+missing display.
+
+Ring map:
+
+```text
+R = Q[h_0_8,h_0_7,h_0_6,h_0_5,h_0_4,h_0_3,h_0_2,h_0_1,h_0_0,
+      bp,bq,br,bs,c,T]
+variables x,y are polynomial variables eliminated by coefficient extraction.
+
+h = y^8(y-x) + h_0_8 y^8 + h_0_7 y^7 + ... + h_0_1 y + h_0_0
+A = (h - h|_{y=0})/y
+beta = bp A + bq y + br x + bs
+f = h^2 + 2 beta
+alpha = quotient_y(beta^2, h)
+g = h^3 + 3 beta h + (3/2) alpha
+E_A = coefficients of J_{x,y}(f,g) - c x^4
+saturate by T c - 1.
+```
+
+The extracted `E_A` has 29 generators.  The first generator is `-c`, and
+therefore the saturated ideal has the explicit certificate
+`1 = -(T c - 1) - T*(-c)`.  Singular's reduced basis is `[1]`.
+The unsaturated ideal without `T c - 1` is nontrivial, so the wrapper control
+is not vacuous.
+
+Branch B exact Moh system.  COUNTING-BOUND[SOURCE-OMITTED].  Moh prints
+`Omega`, five leading terms, `J=x`, and the count 11; he does not print the
+11 variables or equations.  I did not invent monomial support from the leading
+terms alone.
+
+Branch C, missing `1+1+1` cubic partition.  COUNTING-BOUND[SOURCE-OMITTED].
+The page excludes it by assertion only: "precisely two roots" is printed, but
+no local hypothesis check or coefficient exclusion is displayed.  No
+corresponding `Omega` normal form or system is in pp.207--211.
+
+## Solver Results
+
+MEASURED, driver `box/moh9966-20260903/moh9966_branch_driver.py`.
+All Singular runs used the same ring controls requested in the prompt:
+`<c,Tc-1>` must be empty and `<c-1,Tc-1>` must be nonempty.
+
+| branch | system | unknowns | equations | mod 32003 | mod 32009 | mod 32027 | exact Q |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|
+| A LINEAR-POWER | A/B predecessor for `(27,18;21;8;X^4)` | 14 plus `T` | 29 plus `Tc-1` | SATURATED-EMPTY | SATURATED-EMPTY | SATURATED-EMPTY | SATURATED-EMPTY, basis size 1 |
+| B TWO-ROOT-CUBIC | Moh omitted `Omega` 11-variable system | 11 printed, not identified | not printed | NOT-RUN/SOURCE-OMITTED | NOT-RUN/SOURCE-OMITTED | NOT-RUN/SOURCE-OMITTED | COUNTING-BOUND[SOURCE-OMITTED] |
+| C THREE-SIMPLE-ROOT-CUBIC | missing partition system | none printed | none printed | NOT-RUN/SOURCE-OMITTED | NOT-RUN/SOURCE-OMITTED | NOT-RUN/SOURCE-OMITTED | COUNTING-BOUND[SOURCE-OMITTED] |
+
+Branch A exact controls:
+
+```text
+CONTROL_EMPTY_PASS      for <c,Tc-1>
+CONTROL_NONEMPTY_PASS   for <c-1,Tc-1>
+MAIN_START equations=29 unknowns=14 char=0
+MAIN_DONE basis_size=1
+MAIN_SATURATED_EMPTY
+UNSATURATED_Q_CONTROL: NONTRIVIAL, basis_size=14
+```
+
+JSON result SHA-256:
+`ceb2625c8b8c27f07491242a9982d834c5a495a8db678eb5af6cb878dc76e215`.
+
+## Verdict
+
+TYPE: I cannot state "no Keller pair with the `(99,66)` skeleton" from this
+lane.  The computable branch-A predecessor dies, but branch B and the missing
+`1+1+1` cubic partition do not have source-specified systems to saturate.
+They are not SURVIVES and not live representatives; they are
+COUNTING-BOUND[SOURCE-OMITTED].  No direct Jacobian point exists to print.
+
+Scope:
+
+```text
+PROVED-HERE: branch A A/B predecessor for Moh's transformed linear-power row
+             has no c!=0 solution.
+SOURCE-ASSERTED: p.209 dichotomy and "precisely two roots".
+OPEN: exact Moh ten-coefficient branch-A eta system as printed nowhere;
+      exact Moh 11-variable Omega system; 1+1+1 cubic exclusion.
+NOT CLAIMED: n<=100 theorem, full actual minor-radius attainment, or a
+             counterexample candidate.
+```
+
+FALLACY-v2 check: major radii, the p.209 radius-2 `g` probe, and the actual
+combined minor radius are kept separate.  Saturation extracts the ideal
+component in the declared ring and has positive/negative wrapper controls.
+No new exit-price assertion is made, hence no `charge_basis` line.
+
+## D=108 Readiness
+
+The same scaffold is not ready to run on `(108,72)` without a replacement for
+Moh's p.209 probe.  Exact arithmetic for that row:
+
+```text
+n=108, m=72
+M_1..M_3=(-72,81,106)
+d_1..d_4=(108,36,9,1)
+V_2,V_3=(7,7)
+u_3=2,  v_3/u_3=7/2
+major (delta_1,delta_2,delta_3)=(3/8,1/4,-1)
+```
+
+What replaces the radius-2 probe is not another fixed radius.  It must be an
+actual minor-disc first-separation datum `rho=delta_2^*` for the combined
+cluster of `g,T_1^psi,T_2^psi,T_3^psi`, with the leading polynomials at that
+same `rho`.  If `rho >= 7/2`, Prop.6.3 can be invoked.  If `rho < 7/2`, then
+`ord g(sigma_rho)=12(2 rho-7)<0`, and the detector polynomial has degree 2
+with partitions one double root or two simple roots; those case-specific
+systems would then have to be derived.  Prop.6.1 alone gives only
+`delta_2^* >= 1`, which is below `7/2`.
+
